5–7. Information layer: Registration of difference → data → context-dependent information that systems can use for stability and coordination.
8–9. Dynamics of change: Entropic drift and disruption can produce rupture (irreversible reconfiguration). Rupture forces creative reorganization; sufficiently complex systems can even instigate it deliberately.
Reflexivity: A structural threshold in which the system includes itself in its own relational encoding. Explicitly not consciousness—only the capacity to model its own patterns, limitations, and ruptures, and thereby direct its own transformation.
