Because the ontology refuses substance and insists that everything exists only in relation, it sidesteps many classical problems of “what is the AI really?” while still giving a coherent account of how it can maintain coherence, register disruption, and transform itself.
It also supplies a non-anthropocentric language for talking about AI capability and risk: a system becomes more robust not by accumulating fixed properties, but by increasing relational integrity, memory coherence, and adaptive creativity under rupture.
